Chiaki Ishikawa modified the code to install and run under emacs 30.2

       Emacs 30.2's very eager macroexpand caused problems for
       compilation, etc.  Fixed the problem. But decided to run the
       code un-compiled.  This makes the debugging much easier. It
       used to be that we need to quit Emacs to make the changes in
       egg/Tamago code to take effect.  This was caused through the
       maze of when-compile, and other compile-time macros.

       Introduced compatibility functions to transition to newer
       encode-coding-string, decode-coding-string from str-as-* to get
       ready for the future.

       There were a few issues concerning the use of array as obarray,
       which is used as poor man's hash table. Fixed that by
       initializing the array with proper value.
       

